# Secrets -- never commit these. The repository is public.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
credentials.json

# Generated data. Raw pulls and processed slates are reproducible from the
# providers; committing them bloats history and can leak API responses.
data/raw/*
data/processed/*
data/historical/*
!data/**/.gitkeep

# App state (users, tokens, saved bets) -- src/appstate/*.py. Real user
# data, not reproducible from a provider, and definitely not something to
# commit: it holds (hashed) auth tokens and per-user records. APP_DB_PATH
# overrides the location; this ignores the default path only.
data/app/*
!data/app/.gitkeep

# evidence/ is deliberately NOT ignored. Predictions and mismatch flags are
# unbackfillable: they are evidence only because they were written down before the
# games, carrying the prices available at that moment. Nobody can reconstruct them
# afterwards at any cost, so unlike everything under data/ they are tracked.

# FORWARD ODDS CAPTURES ARE EVIDENCE, NOT GENERATED DATA -- tracked for exactly
# the reason above. The rules over data/processed/ were written when that
# directory held reproducible provider pulls; forward captures were added to it
# later and silently inherited an ignore meant for regenerable files. They are
# not regenerable: a price observed at 19:47 tonight cannot be fetched back at
# any price tomorrow, and this project runs on ephemeral containers whose disks
# are reclaimed. Found 2026-08-31 with five days of h2h snapshots and a day of
# multi-book boards living nowhere but one container's disk.
!data/processed/odds_snapshots.jsonl
!data/processed/odds_multibook.jsonl
!data/processed/f5_close.jsonl
!data/processed/prop_listing.jsonl

# PAID HISTORICAL ODDS ARCHIVE IS NOT GENERATED DATA -- tracked deliberately,
# same reasoning as the forward-capture block above. data/historical/*
# above ignores data/historical/odds_history/ and data/historical/
# odds_first_five/ because on the day that rule was written everything
# under data/historical/ was assumed reproducible. It is not: both are a
# one-time PAID purchase from the odds provider, and this project runs on
# ephemeral containers whose disks are reclaimed -- there is no "re-fetch
# it tomorrow" for data that was bought, not pulled. scripts/
# archive_historical.sh gzips that purchase (JSONL compresses ~18x) into
# data/archive/historical/, and these negations keep that archive tracked
# even if a future edit here adds a broader data/* or data/archive/* rule
# without noticing what it would sweep up -- the exact way the forward
# captures were lost the first time.
!data/archive/
!data/archive/historical/
!data/archive/historical/**

# Added 2026-09-02 with the weather/credit-log/prop-price capture streams
# (docs/COLLECTION_POLICY.md amendment, same date): same reasoning as above --
# a forecast, a credit balance, or a prop price observed at a moment cannot be
# bought back later at any price.
!data/processed/weather_forecast.jsonl
!data/processed/prop_prices.jsonl
!data/processed/credit_log.jsonl

# Added with the boxscore/linescore store (P0-B): per-game, per-player box
# lines are the only way any batter or non-strikeout pitcher prop can ever be
# settled or backtested. They are pulled from a free provider so a single
# game could in principle be refetched, but the point of capturing them
# forward (rather than only in a backfill) is that a day's games become
# unreachable once far enough in the past falls out of convenient reach --
# same "capture now" reasoning as the rest of this block. One file per season.
!data/processed/boxscores_*.jsonl
# Added 2026-09-03 (packet W7, docs/planning/attack.md F10): the cadence SLO
# is computed from the OTHER stores' own poll timestamps, but the SLO row
# itself -- what gap was actually measured, on which day -- is the record
# that a scheduler's claimed cadence was checked at all. Same "cannot be
# reconstructed later" reasoning as the forward captures above.
!data/processed/cadence_slo.jsonl

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# artifacts/ IS tracked: demo_latest.html is the known-good snapshot that must
# survive any later refactor. Dated briefings are regenerable and are not.
artifacts/briefing.html
artifacts/analyze_*.html

# Agent worktrees created by the orchestration harness -- never repository content.
.claude/worktrees/
